@startuml
' purpose: Stop persistence checkpoints versus best-effort OpenCode idle synchronization
' covers: packages/lib/hooks/git-sync-turn.sh
' covers: packages/lib/hooks/proveo-git-sync-turn.js
' covers: packages/lib/entrypoint-lib.sh
' covers: defs/opencode/entrypoint.sh
' covers: defs/cursor/defaults/hooks.json
' covers: defs/base/Dockerfile
' covers: defs/cursor/Dockerfile
' covers: defs/opencode/Dockerfile
' covers: defs/codex/Dockerfile
' covers: defs/codex/managed/requirements.toml
' covers: defs/claudecode/mcp/Dockerfile
' covers: internal/contract/git_sync_turn_test.go
' covers: internal/contract/opencode_runtime_test.go
' covers: internal/contract/testdata/opencode_git_sync_plugin.mjs
' covers: e2e/git_sync_turn_test.go
' Approved OpenCode plugin migration: _spec/defs/opencode/native-v2-integration.puml
' The native plugin, --standalone helper and headless --auto are implemented;
' primary reports focused plugin/runtime contracts passed. Full live acceptance is
' tracked by the native sibling: model-driven idle commit/push in actual sbx remains
' unexecuted because sbx/tooling is unavailable, not because fixture work is pending.
' OpenCode synchronization is eventual in a live session; neither idle observation
' nor hook failure gates CLI return. Do not assert commit/push before run exits.
'
' A failed `git add` names git's own first "error:" line in the block reason.
' A bare "git add failed" (seen 2026-09-29 in proveo-claudecode-1b3fcb7f, whose
' clone and trace were gone with the sandbox) left the agent guessing at a
' cause the hook had in hand. TestGitSyncNamesWhyGitAddFailed pins it.
'   seed step order ............... _spec/packages/lib/seed-and-launch.puml
'   live e2e per def .............. _spec/tests/44-git-sync-turn-e2e.puml
'   git identity .................. _spec/internal/gitidentity/authorship.puml
' Notes are capped at 5 lines x 50 columns; one idea per anchor.
' Register: manual normalized word/syllable counts; two sentences per rewritten note.
' FK: note right of HOOK; words=30 syllables=55; FK 11.9
' FK: note over HOOK (N_RECURSE); words=32 syllables=55; FK 10.9
' FK: note over OC (N_RACE); words=32 syllables=58; FK 12.0
' Historical startup measurement: sbx launched OpenCode six seconds before the plugin
' seed copied it. The current release boundary includes native config and agents,
' not just the older hooks-only marker; tool provisioning need not gate release.
!include https://raw.githubusercontent.com/proveo-ca/identity/main/proveo.puml
skinparam noteTextAlignment left
title git-sync-turn — Stop checkpoint / best-effort idle observer

participant "Claude / Codex\nStop" as STOP <<app>>
participant "Cursor stop" as CU <<app>>
participant "OpenCode\nsession.idle" as OC <<app>>
participant "git-sync-turn.sh" as HOOK <<app>>
participant "git commit / push" as GIT <<app>>
participant "block / followup" as BLOCK <<error>>

STOP ARROW_MAIN HOOK : stdin JSON
CU ARROW_MAIN HOOK : stdin JSON
OC ARROW_QUEUE HOOK : idle notification, best-effort
HOOK ARROW_MAIN GIT
GIT ARROW_MAIN HOOK : clean or pushed
HOOK ARROW_MAIN STOP : no decision / {}
GIT ARROW_ERROR BLOCK : identity or push miss
BLOCK ARROW_QUEUE STOP : reason as next prompt
BLOCK ARROW_QUEUE CU : followup_message

note right of HOOK
  Turn-end hooks give Claude, Cursor, and Codex
  a persistence checkpoint before returning.
  OpenCode observes an idle session, so git sync
  remains best-effort and must never become an
  awaited CLI-return gate.
end note

note over BLOCK
  **One continuation, then rest.** A
  failed persist blocks Stop once.
  stop_hook_active or loop_count>0
  allows stop so Claude's 8-cap and
  Cursor's loop_limit cannot trap.
end note

note right of GIT
  **Commit is mechanical.** Push is
  not forced: no --force, --amend,
  or --no-verify. .env, auth.json
  and key files stay unstaged. No
  remote means commit, then allow.
end note

' note-id: N_OFF
note over HOOK
  **Off is a no-op.** Set
  PROVEO_GIT_SYNC=off to skip seed
  and the script. Cursor still bakes
  the stop entry; the script allows.
  An aborted Cursor turn never commits.
end note

' note-id: N_MSG
note over GIT
  **Subject describes the work.** The staged
  diff goes to a light model (Claude: sonnet).
  One retry at 2x timeout; then the subject
  summarises paths. No static subject exists.
end note

' note-id: N_MSG_WHY
note over GIT
  **13 static subjects hid the failure.**
  eda7718..f1eb5a9 (2026-09-24/25) all fell
  back to "persist turn"; the e2e pinned
  MSG=off, so no test saw the model path.
end note

' note-id: N_ISOLATE
note over HOOK
  **claude -p loads CLAUDE.md by default.**
  Measured 2026-10-02: the reply opened with
  "Executor," from AGENTS.md. The call runs
  in /, --setting-sources "", --tools "",
  diff on stdin. --bare drops OAuth: unused.
end note

' note-id: N_MSG_KNOBS
note over GIT
  PROVEO_GIT_SYNC_MODEL_* overrides the model;
  PROVEO_GIT_SYNC_MSG=off skips the call and the
  commit still happens. Cursor has no verified
  small-model id: unset MODEL_CURSOR = skip.
end note

' note-id: N_RECURSE
note over HOOK
  Nested subject generation can load the live
  session's hooks and recurse into git sync.
  The native OpenCode migration adds
  ""--standalone"" to that helper while retaining
  the inflight guard across every harness call.
end note

' note-id: N_INFLIGHT
note over HOOK
  PROVEO_GIT_SYNC_MSG_INFLIGHT=1 is set on the
  child and checked first thing on entry.
end note

note over OC
  **Idle must not inherit the TTY.**
  The script opened with cat. On a
  TTY that never EOFs, so every key
  after session.idle went to cat.
  Plugin: </dev/null. Script: skip TTY.
end note
' note-id: N_DIALECT
note over STOP, CU
  **Allow is silence.** Claude and Codex Stop
  accept "block" or no decision; "allow" is a
  schema error shown as "Stop hook error".
  Cursor still takes {}.
end note

' note-id: N_CODEX
note over STOP
  **Codex hooks are managed, not user.** User
  hooks.json waits for /hooks review, so an
  unattended turn never ran it. The image
  bakes /etc/codex/requirements.toml instead.
end note

' note-id: N_LAZY
note over OC
  **Bun's $ is lazy.** An unawaited
  ShellPromise never spawns; the idle plugin
  ran nothing. Measured 2026-09-24 in
  proveo-opencode-c1c4da74 with a probe plugin.
end note

' note-id: N_RACE
note over OC
  Plugin discovery happens at launch, so the seed
  must install hooks before releasing the agent.
  Release also follows native config and agent
  rendering, while tool provisioning can continue
  after the CLI starts.
end note

' note-id: N_CLONE
note over GIT
  **A read-only origin is commit-only.** In an
  sbx clone origin is /run/sandbox/source (ro).
  Push there always failed; teardown already
  fetches the commit into refs/proveo/<sid>/.
end note
@enduml
